# Wave W17-Y (Vernal Path): bloom turf — bloom-lane turf, bank flecks: a soft olive-green lane turf carrying pink and white petal flecks shed off the flower banks, quieter than any meadow (design: the lane the seasons use, unbroken flower banks either side; the shipped flower banks stand byte-preserved in this ground’s field and the ground converts around them). The Vernal Path’s own ground — split from its twin Route 214 by hush entire (the lane vs the open meadow road) and from Farewell Spring’s spring meadow ahead by motion: petals fall here, the spring is still.
